# Effects — Visual Node Editor for GPU Image Pipelines

## What This Is

A browser-based visual node editor for building GPU image-effect pipelines. Users create processing graphs by wiring nodes on a React Flow canvas; each node is backed by a **processor** that runs shader / compute logic via PixiJS (WebGL2) and publishes typed outputs downstream. The engine executes the entire graph every frame in topological order, enabling real-time preview of multi-pass shader effects, segmentation, contour extraction, and animation.

The app is a single-page tool — there is one route (`/`) that renders the `NodeEditor`.

> **Maintenance contract (every agent reads this).** This document and `product-vision.mdc` are the canonical map of the codebase. They are part of the deliverable. Whenever you finish a task that changes processor count, effect catalog, slot layout, persistence shape, directory layout, snapshot schema, animation pool semantics, or any other invariant described here — **update the affected sections of these two files in the same change**. Out-of-date rules cost more debugging time than the documentation update. If you intentionally diverge from a rule, rewrite the rule; do not leave the codebase contradicting it.

