## Processor System (`node-engine/processors/`)

### BaseProcessor (abstract)

- `def: ProcessorDef` — type, title, category, input/output handles, defaultParams.
- `execute(inputs, params, engine) → Record<string, any>` — pure computation per frame.
- `alwaysDirty: boolean` — if `true`, the engine marks this node dirty every frame.
- RT management: `ensureRT(w, h)`, `ensurePing(w, h)`, `ensurePong(w, h)` — reuses `RenderTexture` when dimensions match, destroys on resize.
- `val(inputs, params, key, fallback)` — priority: connected input > widget param > fallback.
- `resolveRes(inputs, params, engine)` — resolution priority: explicit width/height > `source` texture > `sdf`/`coords_tex` > any texture > engine defaults (900x1200).

### Slot Types

`TEXTURE`, `NUMBER`, `VEC`, `CONFIG`, `CONTOUR`, `EVENT`, `SIGNAL`, `ANIMATION`, `METRICS`, `TEXT`, `TEXT_STYLE`, `ANY` (wildcard). Connection validation uses `SLOT_COMPAT` table in `node-editor/constants.ts`. `TEXT_STYLE` is intentionally distinct from `CONFIG` so users can't accidentally wire a typography preset into an effect's `config` input. There is no separate `POLYGON` slot — geometry flows as `CONTOUR` (ContourSamples SoA) end-to-end; the legacy `polygon` processor that packed raw points into a coords texture has been removed.

### Signal Types

- `EventSignal` — discrete event: `{ count, lastTimestampMs, lastX?, lastY? }`.
- `Signal` — continuous driver from Timer / Interpolator / Envelope / Combine: `{ value, time, age, state, lastTimestampMs }`. `value` is the user-controlled waveform output (clamped or unbounded depending on mode); `time` is the source-internal monotonic ms clock and is **not** propagated to shaders directly — see "Animation Channels" below.
- `ChannelSignal` — per-channel packet emitted by `AnimationController`: `{ time, raw, value, state }`. Note: `time` here carries the upstream `Signal.value` (unclamped), **not** the upstream `Signal.time` ms — keeping it as user-controlled drive is what makes a paused Timer actually freeze the channel and `unbounded` mode grow it linearly.
- `AnimationSignal` — `{ channels: Record<string, ChannelSignal> }`.
- `EffectMetrics` — per-frame profiler payload from EffectProcessor: `{ effectName, totalMs, cpuMs, gpuDispatchMs, passes: PassMetric[], timestampMs }`. `PassMetric` carries `{ id, kind, cpuMs, skipped }`.

### Processor Categories & Catalog (27 types)

**Input** (6): `number`, `constantSignal`, `image`, `text`, `textStyle`, `textStrip`
**Image ops** (4): `blur`, `remap`, `blend`, `denoise`
**Contour** (3): `segmentation` (TEXTURE → CONTOUR via SAM), `contourResample` (Chaikin/Laplacian smoothing, arc-length resampling), `sdfFromContour` (CONTOUR → SDF TEXTURE)
**Animation triggers** (2): `eventEmitter` (on-demand EventSignal source — EMIT button, no canvas listener), `timer` (linear-phase time source: looped saw or unbounded growth, with `paused` toggle)
**Animation modulators** (4): `envelope` (event → shaped signal), `interpolator` (signal → profile-shaped signal: linear/sine/triangle/bell/gaussian/pulse), `combineSignals` (add/max/min/mul/mix), `signalSwitch` (two SIGNALs cross-faded by an EVENT control — each event toggles A↔B with separate A→B / B→A duration + easing profiles)
**Animation controllers** (2): `animationController` — universal 8-slot mapper. Inputs `signal_0..signal_7` (raw 0..1) plus optional `config` (CONFIG, supplies per-effect slot labels and default min/max). Output `animation: AnimationSignal` keyed by index strings `'0'..'7'`. Per-slot params `min_i`/`max_i`. (Output handle is named `animation` — not `signal` — so it doesn't visually collide with the SIGNAL-typed `signal` outputs of Timer / Interpolator / Combine / SignalSwitch.) `animationSwitch` — two-input cross-fade between two whole AnimationSignal packets, gated by a discrete EVENT, with per-direction transition duration + easing profile (same UX as `signalSwitch` but applied to every channel of the pool at once); use to swap whole controller presets on a single Emit instead of fanning out 8 SignalSwitches.
**Output** (3): `effect` (multi-pass shader compositor; emits `texture` + `metrics`), `preview` (pass-through + canvas extract), `contourPreview`
**Utility** (3): `config` (effect selection + params passthrough), `noiseVisualizer` (pattern-warp preview of canonical fbm), `log` (effect timing inspector)

#### Text composition

Text rendering used to be a single self-contained node (`textStrip` baking text + font + spacing into its own params). It is now decomposed into three nodes that communicate through the typed `TEXT` and `TEXT_STYLE` slots:

- `text` — emits `text: TEXT`. Single multiline string param. One source can feed several Text Strips with the same copy.
- `textStyle` — emits `style: TEXT_STYLE` (`{ font, letterSpacing, weight: 'regular' | 'bold', transform: 'none' | 'upper' | 'lower' }`). One preset can drive several Text Strips at once.
- `textStrip` — consumes `text: TEXT` (required) + `style: TEXT_STYLE` (optional, falls back to a sensible default). Emits a single `texture` output; downstream consumers derive the strip aspect ratio from `texture.width / texture.height` (Effect already exposes this as `uTxcn{i}Aspect`).

The previous `sdfTextAtlas` processor was removed (no live effect consumed it). Old snapshots that contain it will log `Unknown processor type: sdfTextAtlas` from `DataflowEngine.addNode` and skip it — this is intentional, the editor does not auto-migrate. Text-using snapshots saved before the split also stop rendering until the user wires the new pair of source nodes; this is the agreed clean break.

#### Geometry composition

Polygon-shaped data is `CONTOUR` end-to-end. There is no `POLYGON` slot any more.

- `segmentation` emits `contour: CONTOUR` directly — it builds a full `ContourSamples` packet (positions + tangents + arcS + totalLength + aabb + closed) from the raw SAM polygon point list and caches it by reference, so consumers can plug it straight into `contourPreview`, `contourResample`, `sdfFromContour`, or the Effect node's `contour` input without an intermediate adapter.
- `contourResample` now takes `contour: CONTOUR` and emits a single `contour: CONTOUR` (smoothing + uniform / curvature-adaptive resampling + optional outward offset). Its previous secondary outputs (`smoothed_polygon: POLYGON`, `total_length: NUMBER`) had no live consumers and were dropped — the totalLength lives on `ContourSamples` itself.
- The legacy `polygon` processor (file-loaded JSON polygon → `coords_tex` / `aabb` / `point_count` / `tex_dim` outputs that the SDF stage used to read) was removed. SDF generation now goes through `sdfFromContour`, which builds the coords texture internally from `ContourSamples`. The dead `coords_tex` / `aabb` / `point_count` / `tex_dim` reads have been deleted from `effect.ts`, `EffectInputName`, `BaseProcessor.resolveRes`, and `pipeline/uniforms.ts` (`applyCoordsUniforms` and the JSON-input `buildCoordsTexture` are gone).

The depth-estimation (`depthEstimate`, `depthBlit`) and AI material/normals processors (`materialEstimate`, `marigoldDepth`, `marigoldNormals`) used to ship in the catalog but were removed. Their category strings (`depth`, `ai`, `marigold`, `dnf`, `source`, `process`) are still tolerated by `ProcessorDef.category` and `categoryColors.ts` as **legacy aliases** so old persisted snapshots continue to load with sensible accent colours; do not remove these aliases until snapshot migration is in place.

**`alwaysDirty` processors**: `effect`, `eventEmitter`, `timer`, `envelope`, `combineSignals`, `signalSwitch`, `animationController`, `animationSwitch`. `interpolator` is intentionally **not** alwaysDirty — it's a pure function of its input and rides upstream propagation (Timer / Envelope / Combine are alwaysDirty). The `log` processor relies on dirty-propagation from upstream Effect — it's not alwaysDirty itself, so an unwired Log node sits idle and adds zero per-frame cost.

#### Animation composition (Timer + Interpolator)

The previous monolithic `autoTimer` baked clock + waveform into a single node. It is now decomposed into two complementary processors:

- `timer` — pure time source. Two modes: `looped` (phase wraps `[0, 1)` every `durationMs`, saw-tooth with instant reset) and `unbounded` (`elapsed / durationMs`, grows linearly forever, ideal for monotonic shader scroll consumers). Carries `phaseOffsetMs` for staggering and a `paused` toggle that freezes the elapsed-ms accumulator without losing phase.
- `interpolator` — shape-only complement. Consumes a SIGNAL whose `.value` is a phase, applies one of `linear | sine | triangle | bell | gaussian | pulse` (mirroring the original autoTimer modes minus `constant`), and emits a SIGNAL whose `.value` is the shaped curve sampled at `phase = frac(input.value)`. `linear` profile is a passthrough that preserves unbounded inputs intact. Pure function of input → not `alwaysDirty`.

Minimal animation graph: `Timer → AnimationController → Effect`. Insert an `Interpolator` between the Timer and the controller (or anywhere downstream of any SIGNAL source) when you want a shaped waveform; omit it for raw monotonic phase. To freeze a channel: `Timer.paused = true` (combine with `phaseOffsetMs` for any static phase). Old snapshots referencing `autoTimer` log `Unknown processor type: autoTimer` from `DataflowEngine.addNode` and skip — the editor does not auto-migrate; rebuild the chain manually.

