## UI Architecture

### NodeEditor.tsx

Orchestrates everything: `useNodesState` + `useEdgesState` (React Flow), `engineRef` (DataflowEngine), four custom hooks, toolbar, sidebar, context menu. Loading gate shows "Initializing GPU..." until Pixi is ready.

### BaseNodeShell.tsx

Wraps every node view. Renders: `NodeResizer` (visible when selected, grid-snapped), coloured header (accent from category via CSS `--pn-accent`), input/output `<Handle>`s at 20px row pitch (aligned to editor grid), widget area, pin toggle button.

Two modes: **graph** (full chrome + handles) and **headless** (no handles/resizer — used in pin sidebar).

### EditableStepEdge.tsx

Custom orthogonal edge with draggable bend points. Segments snap to grid. Bend data persists in `edge.data.bends`. Supports selection, deletion, and hover states.

### Node Views (`views/`)

24 components, one per processor type. Each wraps `BaseNodeShell` and renders parameter widgets using the `widgets/` components. They access the engine via `useEngine()` and update params via `useSetParam()`.

### Category Colours

8 live hues with intentional progression: green (input) → gold/orange/pink (animTrigger / animMod / animCtrl) → blue (imageOp) → teal (contour) → red (output) → slate (util). 6 legacy aliases (`depth` sky, `ai`/`marigold`/`dnf` violet, `source` green, `process` blue) keep persisted scenes from going grey but do not appear in the live menu. All accents sit on the dark side of the perceived-luminance line so the unified light header text reads cleanly without per-colour overrides.

